%I A401519 #15 Nov 26 2026 15:12:16
%S A401519 1,8,32,104,312,800,1824,3952,7944,14880,26960,46880,78344,128168,
%T A401519 204176,317280,484416,723600,1060752,1531792,2175760,3044464,4209616,
%U A401519 5743304,7740712,10323320,13609584,17764888,22993920,29452312,37451120,47195464,59125896
%N A401519 Expansion of g.f. Phi^4*F^4, where Phi = g.f. for A028930 and F = g.f. for A028959.
%C A401519 a(n) is the number of representations of n by the 16-variable quadratic form that is the sum of 4 copies of 2*x^2 + x*y + 3*y^2 and 4 copies of x^2 + x*y + 6*y^2.
%H A401519 Karan Sharma, <a href="/A401519/b401519.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A401519 Bülent Köklüce, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11139-013-9480-4">Cusp forms in S_6(Gamma_0(23)), S_8(Gamma_0(23)) and the number of representations of numbers by some quadratic forms in 12 and 16 variables</a>, Ramanujan J. 34 (2014), 187-208. See p. 204.
%o A401519 (PARI) th(M, N) = 1 + 2*x*Ser(qfrep(M, N, 1), x);
%o A401519 a(n) = polcoef(th([4, 1; 1, 6], n+1)^4 * th([2, 1; 1, 12], n+1)^4, n);
%Y A401519 Cf. A028930, A028959, A328527, A328528, A328529, A328530, A328531, A328532, A328533, A328534, A328535, A328536, A401430, A401474, A402729, A402730.
%K A401519 nonn,new
%O A401519 0,2
%A A401519 _Karan Sharma_, Nov 26 2026
